Stomata have daily rhythms of opening and closing.

Fig. 6.1 shows the percentage of stomata open at different times of the day, over a period of three days, in the thale cress plant, *Arabidopsis thaliana*.

{{figure:figure-6-1.webp}}

parts.text:
Table 6.1 shows some of the events occurring during the closure of a stoma.

The events are **not** listed in the correct order.

{{figure:reviewed_table_1.png}}

Complete Table 6.2 to show the correct order of the events shown in Table 6.1.

Three of the events have been completed for you.

